---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Nav from "../../components/Nav/Nav.astro";
import ContentPage from "../../components/ContentPage/ContentPage.astro";
import Footer from "../../components/Footer/Footer.astro";
import { getSite } from "../../data/site";

const lang = "en";
const site = getSite(lang);
---

<Layout
  lang={lang}
  title="CODE OF CONDUCT — IV Devs"
  description="IV Devs community guidelines: a safe, inclusive, and respectful space for everyone."
>
  <Nav lang={lang} />

  <ContentPage lang={lang} title="CODE OF CONDUCT" eyebrow="// CONDUCT">
    <p>
      One of IV Devs' main goals is to be <strong>inclusive</strong> for as many
      contributors as possible, with the greatest diversity of backgrounds. We
      are committed to providing a pleasant, safe, and welcoming environment for
      everyone, regardless of sex, sexual orientation, ability, ethnicity,
      socioeconomic status, and religion.
    </p>
    <p>
      This code summarizes our expectations for everyone who participates in the
      community, as well as the consequences of unacceptable behavior.
    </p>

    <h2>Expected behavior</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Participate authentically and actively.</li>
      <li>
        Practice consideration and respect in your communications and actions.
      </li>
      <li>Try to collaborate instead of creating conflict.</li>
      <li>Be aware of your surroundings and of other participants.</li>
      <li>
        Alert the organizers if you notice a risky situation or a violation of
        this code.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Unacceptable behavior</h2>
    <p>
      We do not tolerate intimidation, harassment, abuse, discrimination, or
      derogatory communication, whether online or at any of our events.
      Harassment includes harmful comments related to gender, sexual
      orientation, race, religion, or disability; sexual images in public
      spaces; deliberate intimidation; stalking; non-consensual photography or
      recording; sustained interruption of talks; inappropriate physical contact
      and unwelcome sexual attention.
    </p>

    <h2>Consequences</h2>
    <p>
      Anyone asked to stop unacceptable behavior is expected to do so
      immediately. Organizers may take any action they deem appropriate,
      including a temporary ban or permanent expulsion from the community.
    </p>

    <h2>If you witness or experience something</h2>
    <p>
      Contact a meetup organizer as soon as possible or email us at
      <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>. If an organizer creates
      an inappropriate situation, they will be held to a higher standard.
    </p>

    <h2>Moderation</h2>
    <p>
      Organizers will respond first with a warning. If the warning is ignored,
      the person will be removed from the channel to reflect, or asked to leave
      the venue for 30 minutes at in-person events. If they return and continue
      causing problems, they will be indefinitely removed from the group, event,
      or Slack.
    </p>

    <h2>Scope</h2>
    <p>
      We expect all participants to follow this code in every virtual and
      in-person space of the community. Let's take care of each other: technical
      excellence is not enough, we also have to be the best person we can be.
    </p>

    <p class="text-sm text-dim">
      Adapted from the community Code of Conduct and distributed under the
      Creative Commons BY-SA license.
    </p>
  </ContentPage>

  <Footer lang={lang} />
</Layout>
